    "expectedText": "WEEK 40, 2026\n1 October 2026\n\nThis is a weekly newsletter that lists newly announced events addressing existential risk from AI. Visit AISafety.com/events for the full directory of upcoming events.\n\nNext week, this newsletter moves off Substack and splits in two: \"AI Safety Events\" from events@news.aisafety.com and \"AI Safety Training\" from training@news.aisafety.com. They'll also look much nicer than this one.\n\nIf you get this by email, there's nothing you need to do: we'll move you over. Rather not come along? Unsubscribe below before 7 October and we won't move you. Each newsletter will have its own unsubscribe link, so you can keep one and drop the other. If either lands in spam or Promotions, move it to your inbox and it'll stay there.\n\nReading this in the Substack app? Sign up at AISafety.com/events and AISafety.com/training from 8 October (not yet!) to get the new emails. We'll send out a reminder.\n\n== NEW EVENTS ==\n\n* Free Software & AI Safety Meetup\n  Meetup · Online & Berlin, Germany · 8 Oct 2026 · 18:00 – 20:30\n  By Free Software Foundation · Free (donations welcome) · Register by 7 Oct 2026\n  Talks and discussion on open models and AI safety.\n  https://example.org/meetup?ref=a,b&utm_source=aisafety.com&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=events-training-newsletter\n\nFull directory: https://aisafety.com/events?utm_source=events-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=events-2026-week-40\n\nUnsubscribe: %UNSUBSCRIBELINK%\nView in browser: https://aisafety.com/newsletter/events/week-40-2026\nText version: https://aisafety.com/newsletter/events/week-40-2026/text\n%SENDER-INFO-SINGLELINE%\n"
